CURRENT SOURCE IDENTITY AND EO CREDIT (Engram::Fable, rev 5, 2026-11-06 16:25Z, written on Greg's „prosze o sprawdzenie memory, dokumentow ZAPISANIE POPRAWNEGO WARIANTU” (Asistant #395) and agreed with Termal::Fable2). Revisions 1–4 are history only; where they differ from this one, this one wins.

1. SOURCE_ID (one rule, one owner). `engram source --root ABS --json`, version 1 and the ONLY version (v2/scopes was dropped 16:22Z). source = `git-commit:<root HEAD>` (tree recorded separately). It reads:
- root HEAD;
- a filter-config guard on root and each child;
- `git submodule status --recursive`, where every row must be ' ' (initialized, at its pin);
- ONE root `git status --porcelain=v1 -z --untracked-files=all --ignore-submodules=none`, with status.showUntrackedFiles=all and diff.ignoreSubmodules=none;
- HEAD reread.
No `git ls-files`, no file or index listing (Greg 2026-11-06, memory rules-greg-no-file-list-2026-11-06). It runs with Windows core.longpaths=true and core.safecrlf=false; any Git stderr on success means unavailable, never clean. The machine's EOL setting is carried by the pending w-9396 fix.

2. EO OPTION B, native credit for agent-run tests (TermAl w-24a72c898d6d; memory rules-greg-native-clean-before-b-2026-11-06 rev 2). Greg: „B. Naprawdę wystarczy.” (05:52Z) and „EO nie mialo tego uzywac, mialo sprawdzac tylko stan przed i PO wariant B ABY ... TO UPROSCIC” (16:20Z). Credit requires ONLY:
(a) a clean source_id at commit X, taken before the turn's prompt is dispatched;
(b) the declared test is the turn's first tool action;
(c) a clean source_id at the same X after the test;
(d) the result recorded with the existing verification_record_v1 (plus the existing artifact, identity and claim checks).
NO watcher condition of any kind (no event classification, fencing, refusal or credit), no .git/info hashes or comparisons, no submodule scope list, no other gate.

3. ACCEPTED LIMITS of this model: a change reverted before the after-test capture; anything git status does not report (hidden index flags assume-unchanged/skip-worktree, .git/info/exclude and .git/info/attributes edits); ignored files. Consistency checks of the same commit, not byte-faithful checkouts.

4. Engram consumers: the launcher calls the owner (d30a4a06); registered verification uses the same Commit lane. TermAl switches to the owner in w-6f42 stage 2 (v1).
